menu "E1-Mic module"

    config E1_DEBUG_STREAM
        bool "Enable the raw-audio WebSocket stream"
        default n
        help
            Streams raw PCM over a binary WebSocket, about 93 KiB/s. It was the
            module's only output before the move to MQTT and is kept purely as a
            debugging aid: it is the one way to look at the analog front end's
            waveform from the PC.

            Leave this OFF for the real module. Beyond the bandwidth, a blocking
            send on a busy link starves the ADC pool, which is what caused the
            sample loss seen during the FIS130 bench run.

    config E1_GOERTZEL_WINDOW
        int "Goertzel window, in samples"
        range 256 16384
        default 4096
        help
            Sets both the measurement's noise rejection and how often the module
            reports. At 44.1 kHz, 4096 samples are 93 ms and a 10.8 Hz bin,
            worth about 33 dB against white noise, and produce roughly 10
            reports per second.

            Doubling it buys 3 dB and halves the report rate. It is the only
            knob for that trade-off, so change this rather than adding a
            separate rate limit.

endmenu
